    "physical_description": "Woman's longyi (lower garment) cloth of plain woven and dyed cotton and synthetic blend. With a red body, and the lower portion with horizontal stripes of blue, black, green, yellow and black. The warp ends would have been stitched to form a tube. The longyi tube is worn folded in a large pleat to one side. The excess cloth is tucked in at the waist.",
    "summary": null,
    "historical_context": "Made by the Indha of the Inle Lake area of Shan State. The colour scheme is typical of the cloths worn by Shan women.",
